  "body": "Closes #727\nClaim: mac/m2-lead\n\n### Problem\nThe operator's theme and app-icon requests of 2026-10-28 (theme selector with authors, Legacy / Swift / Rétro 5250 / OG themes, Noël and Samain with their events, 14 July, icon packs, and a guide so agents and humans can submit a theme or an icon by PR) were drafted in a design session on the Mac and never filed. Only a generic LOT-166 (#256) and the legacy icons of LOT-123 reached the tracker.\n\n### Change\n- `docs/THEMES.md` (theme contract: model, tokens, decorations, seasonal windows and events, built-in themes and authors, style charter, layouts, submission checklist) and `docs/ICONS.md` (alternate-icon model as shipped by LOT-123, packs and windows, `orange-hfr`, face geometry, checklist). They link to FEAT-010 and the LOT-121/122/123 specs instead of repeating them.\n- Links: AGENTS.md §2 table, README documentation map, CONTRIBUTING §1 item 7.\n- `docs/LOTS.md`: LOT-166 row widened (seasonal engine + Noël, high, Opus → Fable); LOT-188 to LOT-194 added (#729–#735); `tooling/roadmap/lots.json` regenerated (`lots_from_md.py`; `check-lot-deps.py`: 0 violation).\n- `docs/FEATURES.md` FEAT-010 cell and `docs/features/FEAT-010.md` « Lots » line point to LOT-166 and THEMES.md; LOT-180 noted M4 (operator 2026-11-07).\n- **Reference visuals** (operator, 2026-11-10: the 2026-10-28 boards are the latest version, validated): `docs/assets/themes/` (15 boards, the new icons at 1024 px as JPEG and SVG, the Blender renders, the token draft) with a README, and the generators in `tooling/illustrations/`. Left out: the OG board (real member names and topic title) and `noel-redface.svg` (over the 2 MB file limit). Independent leak check: see below.\n\nWhy this wide: one docs issue owns the guides and the lot plan; each lot (#256, #729–#735, #420) brings its own spec, art and code.\n\n### Independent leak check\nA Sonnet agent, given the raw HFR captures and the account file but not the author's conclusions, collected member pseudos (127), topic titles (112), avatar URLs, cookie and hash values and the account pseudos and passwords with its own patterns, searched every committed text file (raw, HTML- and URL-encoded, split tokens) and read the text of all 15 boards. Result after fixes: no member pseudo, topic title, cookie, token, e-mail or local path. Fixed from its first pass: the theme credit carried the name of one of the operator's forum accounts (removed everywhere, five boards regenerated; operator, 2026-11-10: no credit except Legacy) and a private project name (removed). Left out on purpose: the OG board (real member names and a topic title).\n\n### Tests\nDocs and assets only (no `App/` or `Packages/` file): pre-commit green (ShellCheck on `render_all.sh`), `python3 scripts/check-lot-deps.py` (0 violation), `python3 -m unittest scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py` OK, ledger body checked with `tooling/docs/ledger.py check-body`.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-147\nSwiftHFR final: Noël (Noël soft, Noël abusé) selectable 01/12–26/12, Noël soft switched on 01/12–24/12 unless opted out, sleigh arrival with « Oh Oh Oh ! » alert, elves packing and restore of the previous theme; Samain 01/10–31/10 (LOT-191); 14 July overlay (LOT-194); « Thèmes de saison automatiques » and « Animations de saison » settings (docs/THEMES.md §4–§5).\nLegacy ref: ThemeManager.m:213-244; Common.swift:469-473 @ 2440d79; HFRplusAppDelegate.m:627-677 (forced off at :103, :365); ThemeManager.m:213-245; Common.swift:610-627 @ 87fe0d1c\nLot/Feat: LOT-166, LOT-191, LOT-194, FEAT-010\nGap: UX change\nSource: new UX: operator\nH.1: b·operator\n```\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-148\nSwiftHFR final: Picker grouped by pack (Legacy, Beta, X-face, Saisons): the 9 shipped options on their legacy keys and names plus Orange, Classique Blue, Beta rouge, the X-face variations and season icons; dated icons only inside their window, with a one-time « Revenir à l'icône précédente ? » after it (docs/ICONS.md).\nLot/Feat: LOT-123, LOT-189, LOT-190\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
