   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.1, independent of the author), fresh round on 4395b9b0 (after the branch was rebuilt on the operator's decisions of 2026-11-10): REQUEST CHANGES**\n\n1. Medium, `docs/ICONS.md:42`: « no value decided » for `orange-hfr` while the committed tokens and boards use `#F18F18`.\n2. Medium, `docs/LOTS.md:225`: LOT-166 depends on 122 only, yet Noël abusé needs LOT-188's theme model.\n3. Medium: #256 labels and body (easy, low, Sonnet → Opus, « Closes #154 ») contradict the LOT-166 row.\n4. Low: boards vs text: « par ezzz » vs « par Ezzz », `halloween-pumpkin` vs `halloween-jack`, arrival size « 1/4 » vs « a fifth », board footers citing ICONS §3 for what is now §1.\n5. Low: OG themes credited « d'après le forum HFR (thème web) » against the no-credit rule.\n6. Low: `tooling/illustrations/blender/*.py` use `bpy`: Blender requires published scripts to be GPL-compatible; the repository is PolyForm Noncommercial.\n7. Detail: #727 acceptance (« no image committed ») contradicts decision (b); LOTS.md still lists LOT-180 under M5.\n\n**Fixed in d011a784**\n1. `#F18F18` recorded as provisional (2026-10-28 pixel count of `forum_logo.gif`), final once #728 commits the capture.\n2. The LOT-166 row says Noël abusé needs LOT-188 (its last PR); the Noël soft slice does not (#256 plan), so the dependency column stays 122.\n3. Not in this PR: #256's new title, labels and body are ready and wait for the operator's go to edit that issue.\n4. Fixed: tokens `Ezzz`, boards `theme-legacy`, `selectors` and the four icon boards regenerated (footer §1), ICONS uses `halloween-jack`, THEMES says about a quarter of the screen (operator: 1/5 then « légèrement plus gros »).\n5. Fixed: no credit on OG themes (text, tokens, board title).\n6. Fixed by removing the Blender scripts (operator, 2026-11-10); the renders stay; `tooling/illustrations/README.md` says why.\n7. #727 acceptance updated to decision (b). LOT-180's row moves out of M5 in LOT-180's own PR (#420, M4 since 2026-11-07); this PR states no milestone for it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
